<title>UK: StanChart carries on up on Schroder upgrade.</title>
<headline>StanChart carries on up on Schroder upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Standard Chartered Plc continued to advance on Friday on the back of Schroders Securities Thursday upgrade to a &quot;strong buy&quot; from a &quot;buy&quot;, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares put on 19-1/2p to 884-1/2p by 1241 GMT.</p>
<p>Schroders's review of the UK banking sector was bullish on Standard's growth prospects despite expectations that costs will rise in 1997.</p>
<p>Standard is a notoriously volatile stock and Friday's price move was made on a meagre 864,000 shares traded.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
